# =============================================================================
# Narya (C#/.NET rewrite) — environment variables.
#
# Two separate concerns live in this file:
#
# 1. docker-compose.yaml (dev infra: Postgres + Redis) reads POSTGRES_PASSWORD
#    and REDIS_PASSWORD. Both default to `narya-dev` if unset, matching the
#    connection strings baked into src/Narya.Api/appsettings.json — so for
#    local dev you don't need this file at all.
#
# 2. The API itself reads ASP.NET Core configuration from appsettings.json,
#    appsettings.{Environment}.json, then environment variables (highest
#    precedence among those). ASP.NET Core maps a double-underscore in an env
#    var name to a ":" in configuration, so nested keys become:
#      ConnectionStrings__Narya
#      ConnectionStrings__Redis
#      Narya__DashboardToken
#
# Real secrets for local dev do NOT belong in a .env file at all — use
# `dotnet user-secrets set <Key> <Value>` inside src/Narya.Api (UserSecretsId
# is `narya-api`). The double-underscore variables below are documented here
# for the eventual server deploy, where env vars (or a container's secret
# store) are how configuration is actually injected.
# =============================================================================

# --- docker-compose (dev infra) ---------------------------------------------
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=narya-dev
REDIS_PASSWORD=narya-dev

# --- API configuration overrides (server deploy; double-underscore = ":") --
# ConnectionStrings__Narya=Host=localhost;Port=5432;Database=narya;Username=narya;Password=narya-dev
# ConnectionStrings__Redis=localhost:6379,password=narya-dev
# Narya__DashboardToken=
